sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Steinberg (1963, 1970) & Graner-Glazier (1992) differential adhesion cell sorting faithfully reproduces Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 89.9/100, audit 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py; output: docs/media/differential_adhesion_sorting_comparison.png; organism: Chick embryo (Gallus gallus) dissociated tissue aggregates & multicellular embryoid body spheroids; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/654cd6fc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 439c3a9015bc8fdc9014e2aa3a89cd71cffc876fcd81d0cb0b2f88bbf798d5a9; artifact_sha256: 6046cb66ae62af9e47d3b593c06f690c6b389ec313e42183a47ccced8c8cf39f; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-differential-adhesion-sorting-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Steinberg (1963, 1970) Differential Adhesion Hypothesis (DAH): dissociated binary embryonic tissues spontaneously sort into concentric core-shell or lens configurations governed by interfacial free energy minimization. | Graner & Glazier (1992) PRL Eqs. 1-3: extended Cellular Potts Hamiltonian with interfacial tensions gamma_AB = J_AB - (J_AA + J_BB)/2 and gamma_tauM = J_tauM - J_tautau/2 partitioning parameter space into checkerboard (gamma_AB < 0), complete engulfment (0 < gamma_AB < gamma_BM - gamma_AM), partial engulfment (gamma_AB > gamma_BM - gamma_AM > 0), and dissociation (gamma_AM < 0); Fig. 3 reports logarithmically slow decay of the heterotypic boundary length. | Foty, Pfleger, Forgacs & Steinberg (1996) Development Table 1: empirical Gallus gallus tissue surface tensions (20.1 > 12.6 > 8.5 > 4.6 > 1.6 dyn/cm) strictly predict transitive mutual envelopment.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D extended Cellular Potts Model (60^2, 68 cells) across all 5 thermodynamic regimes plus a 7-point continuous J_AB sweep, with a cell-level type-swap accelerator and, in the partial-engulfment regime only, an ad hoc symmetry-breaking field. | Pass 3: 3D extended Cellular Potts spheroid on a 64^3 lattice (840 cells, 26-neighbour adhesion, volume constraint, 8-colour sublattice-parallel Metropolis) with its 2D equatorial z-section, a Kawasaki-swap ablation and a 3D equal-adhesion control; logarithmic vs power-law fits of L_AB(t)/L(t) with exponents compared to the LSW alpha = 1/3 bound. | Computer-vision segmentation of a confocal fluorescence embryoid body spheroid (`cell_sorting_specimen.jpg`) comparing empirical GFP/RFP radial occupancy against the 2D Potts core-shell profile (r = 0.925) and the 3D equatorial-section profile (r = 0.758).; transfer_boundary: 64^3 x 200 MCS is far from the asymptotic coarsening regime; exponents are fitted over ~2.3 decades of MCS including the initial transient, and the power-law vs logarithmic R^2 (0.9965 vs 0.9845 in 3D; 0.737 vs 0.769 in 2D) do not discriminate the two laws. | The LSW alpha = 1/3 reference is a conserved-order-parameter coarsening bound, not an exponent measured for the Cellular Potts model; the Nakajima & Ishihara (2011) exponent is deliberately left null in the reference JSON because the paper could not be consulted offline. | The vendored specimen is a Wikimedia Commons embryoid body, not a chick-tissue aggregate from Steinberg or Foty; the radial-profile comparison is a morphological analogy, not a reproduction of a paper figure.; does_not_claim: Does not model active chemotaxis, subcellular cadherin trafficking kinetics, or the fluctuation-dependence of sorting studied by Mombach et al. (1995). | Does not claim the cell-level type-swap accelerator or the partial-engulfment bias field are part of the Graner & Glazier (1992) Hamiltonian.]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/jez.1401730406>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2007.03.007>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/13/3/033035>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.47.2128>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.69.2013>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.2244>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.141.3579.401>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.122.5.1611> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.899"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "1964-steinberg-differential-adhesion-sorting.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "654cd6fc" .
}

